## Verdicts and fixes

D1 (look-decodable-case, last assertion): REAL. It required `toUpperCase` to stay in
`decodable.tsx`, which AC-1.3 and the P1.4 detector forbid. Change: the self-check now calls the
detector on an in-test string (`const word = text.toUpperCase();`) and on a comment. Non-vacuity:
the real source scan over `app` and `lib` stays, so a shipped `toUpperCase` or CSS `uppercase`
still fails; the self-check proves the detector catches a call and ignores a comment.

D2 (look-reader-highlight, H1): REAL. It asserted more than 100 frames for each single page run;
page 4 has 89 frames. Change: removed the per-run frames detail; the whole-case
`frames_run > 100` guard stays. Non-vacuity: H1 still fails if any page lights a skipped or
out-of-order sequence at any of the four phases.

D3 (look-word-clip-tap, C3): REAL. One mutated week was reused for 8 pages, so `pageBook` cut the
week in place and pages 2 to 8 saw no words (the run stopped at `taps_checked=4`). The tail
compared a clip map with itself. Change: a fresh `allClipsWeek()` per page, and the words are
read from a pristine fixture. The mutant tail now builds real wrong maps (index, first letter,
sentence) and asserts that the taps reject each. Non-vacuity: 33 taps on 8 pages still assert the
exact clip of every word; the mutants fail on real differences (page 3 "sam" vs the index map,
"mia" vs the first-letter map, every non-first word vs the sentence map).

D4 (look-word-clip-tap, C7): REAL. The Thai half never re-installed the rejecting play mock, so a
correct reader could not show the Thai alert. Change: re-install the `NotAllowedError` mock before
the Thai My turn tap. Non-vacuity: the Thai case fails if the alert is absent or wrong; the English
alert, the timer count, and the next-tap clip assertion stay.

D5 (look-word-clip-tap, receiver): REAL. `walk_not_in_list` counted `approval.audio.source`
(provenance text ending in "song.mp3"), which `mediaOf` must not list. Change: skip entries whose
path starts with `approval.`. Non-vacuity: the case still fails if a clip is not listed
(`listed_clips=12`) or if a non-approval media path is missing from `mediaOf`.

D6 (phase3-audio-seek-stop): REAL. The F146 describe was empty after the r3 deletions, and vitest
fails an empty suite with "No test found in suite". Change: removed the empty describe. Non-vacuity:
the other 8 cases (metadata seek, page-end timer, decodable cuts, F140, F145, F153) still run.

## Review of Green's test edits (kept; none weakens an assertion)
- `lib/media/url` mocks in look-week-card-label, look-song-playing, phase3-song-ui,
  look-reader-turn, look-feedback, phase3-loops-off: they supply
  `https://storage.googleapis.com/storytime-app-media/<file>` for every file. The existing
  `endsWith(<file>)` assertions keep their strength; the mock only restores the URL that the login
  task 2b.6 moved to the signed map.
- `lib/media/sign` and `lib/auth` mocks in look-week-card-label and phase3-loops-off: the page
  signs the media and checks a session. The mocks return an empty signed map and a family account.
  The file reads labels only, so no media assertion is weakened.
- phase3-decodable-punct: `NEST` -> `nest` and `NEST.` -> `nest.` This is the AC-1.3 source case,
  not a weakening.
- phase3-loops-off and phase3-audio-seek-stop: one `fireEvent.load` on the second image after a
  Next press, which the task 1.4 hold requires. The page-turn and seek assertions stay.
- Note: phase3-decodable-punct and phase3-loops-off lie outside the allowed paths of closeout
  item 3; the strategy owner should add them to that list.

